  "title": "6. UAS transit through GNSS jamming (Salisbury Plain)",
  "about": "A blue UAS transits west from its ground station to observe a red position on Imber. Red has a fixed GNSS jammer on the high ground, a second on a vehicle moving along the road to the south, an ES/DF pair on the datalink band and a short-range air-defence radar. The worked corridor finds a route and timing that keeps the UAV's GNSS, its datalink to the GCS and its exposure to red ES and radar within bounds.",
